# Alva codename rules and implementation prompt

Status: target specification; the gameplay migration has not yet been implemented.
Inspected baseline: hiyroscript/alva main at 4dce378874eebc6112dfe1ab16f7f20659d3bce4.
This file is intentionally named codename_rule, without an extension.

## Naming contract

Character IDs are four-digit strings, including leading zeroes. 0001 is an example, not a global constant. Animation assets remain under assets/characters/<character_id>/ and retain their actual file extension.

The final numeric suffix is the animation frame number, starting at 1. The number inside attack1 through attack5 identifies the move, not the frame. For example, 0001_attack2_7.png is character 0001, attack 2, frame 7.

| Purpose | Codename / filename stem |
| --- | --- |
| Idle sequence | 0001_idle_1 |
| Run sequence | 0001_run_1 |
| Jump, fall, land | 0001_jump, 0001_fall, 0001_land |
| Ground / airborne hurt | 0001_hurt, 0001_midair_hurt |
| Ground shield preparation, hold, release | 0001_prepshield, 0001_shielding, 0001_releaseshield |
| Numbered attack N (N = 1–5) | 0001_attackN_1 |
| Its airborne variant | 0001_midair_attackN_1 |
| Extra attack | 0001_extra_attack_1 |
| Charge startup | 0001_charge_1 |
| Charge sustained loop | 0001_charge_a, 0001_charge_b |
| Special movement / current dash art | 0001_mouvment_1 |
| Object produced by attack N | 0001_attackN_object_1 |
| Object produced by an airborne attack | 0001_midair_attackN_object_1 |
| Object produced by the extra attack | 0001_extra_attack_object_1 |

Single-pose jump/fall/land/hurt/shield assets may use the exact unsuffixed stems above. A multi-frame version uses _1, _2, etc. Preserve existing frames: 0001 currently has two frames each for jump, fall and land, so these become 0001_jump_1.png and 0001_jump_2.png, and likewise for fall and land. Do not collapse or discard them to match a single-pose example.

Charge always plays its numbered startup once, then alternates charge_a and charge_b while held. Charge release may reuse charge_1, as the current character does; do not create a redundant copy.

Use mouvment exactly as specified for the canonical animation name. Run remains run; special movement does not replace ordinary run. Existing directional input names mouvementLeft/mouvementRight describe controls, not filenames; if normalized to mouvmentLeft/mouvmentRight, migrate every consumer and saved layout key together.

Preserve existing airborne shielding as midair_shielding. For existing dodge sequences use dodge_<frame> and midair_dodge_<frame>; do not merge distinct clips into mouvment or delete unused source artwork.

Runtime move IDs omit the character prefix and frame suffix: attack1, midair_attack1, attack2, midair_attack2, attack3, midair_attack3, attack4, midair_attack4, attack5, midair_attack5, extra_attack. Animation keys use the same vocabulary. Phase subclips can have descriptive keys such as attack4_form, attack4_dash and attack4_release, referencing slices of the canonical attack4 frame series.

